        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Facial rash history and examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Approximately 3–4 weeks of itchy, red, flaky patches around the nostrils, medial eyebrows, and beard line. Worse after hot showers and at the end of the work day. Possible heat/sweat trigger at work in roof spaces. No pain, weeping, crusting, pustules, or systemic symptoms; no new soaps. Examination: erythematous greasy mild scale around the alar folds, brows, glabella, and upper beard line. No pustules or comedones; no rosacea or psoriasis features."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
